          "text": "The pattern is best indexed by a **primitive cubic cell** with \\(a \\approx 10.105\\) \u00c5. The systematic absence of \\(h00\\) reflections with odd \\(h\\), together with the composition and a 40-atom cell (\\(Z=4\\)), points to the ordered chiral space group **\\(P2_13\\) (No. 198)**. Mg and Be are ordered on separate \\(4a\\) sites; Y and Ni each occupy one \\(4a\\) and one \\(12b\\) orbit.\n\nSeveral peaks are split or displaced, particularly near 24.5, 35.3\u201335.5, and 37.5\u00b0, suggesting a minor closely related phase, compositional inhomogeneity, or anisotropic strain. Consequently, the coordinates below should be regarded as the primary powder-derived model and a starting point for Rietveld refinement.\n\n```cif\ndata_Y4MgBeNi4_primary\n_audit_creation_method              'Powder indexing and chemically constrained structure solution'\n_chemical_name_common               'Y4MgBeNi4'\n_chemical_formula_structural        'Y4 Mg Be Ni4'\n_chemical_formula_sum               'Y16 Mg4 Be4 Ni16'\n_cell_formula_units_Z               4\n\n_cell_length_a                      10.1052\n_cell_length_b                      10.1052\n_cell_length_c                      10.1052\n_cell_angle_alpha                   90\n_cell_angle_beta                    90\n_cell_angle_gamma                   90\n_cell_volume                        1032.0\n\n_space_group_crystal_system         cubic\n_space_group_name_H-M_alt           'P 21 3'\n_space_group_IT_number              198\n\n_diffrn_radiation_probe             x-ray\n_diffrn_radiation_wavelength        1.5406\n\nloop_\n_atom_site_label\n_atom_site_type_symbol\n_atom_site_symmetry_multiplicity\n_atom_site_Wyckoff_label\n_atom_site_fract_x\n_atom_site_fract_y\n_atom_site_fract_z\n_atom_site_occupancy\n_atom_site_B_iso_or_equiv\nY1    Y     4   a   0.0968   0.0968   0.0968   1.0   0.50\nY2    Y    12   b   0.0784   0.2897   0.4386   1.0   0.50\nNi1   Ni    4   a   0.3662   0.3662   0.3662   1.0   0.45\nNi2   Ni   12   b   0.1845   0.0318   0.3037   1.0   0.45\nMg1   Mg    4   a   0.6176   0.6176   0.6176   1.0   0.70\nBe1   Be    4   a   0.8621   0.8621   0.8621   1.0   0.70\n```\n\nRepresentative cubic indexing for the principal metric is:\n\n| \\(2\\theta_{\\rm obs}\\) | Approx. \\(hkl\\) |\n|---:|:---|\n| 12.39\u00b0 | 110 |\n| 17.54\u00b0 | 200 |\n| 24.91\u00b0 | 220 |\n| 27.90\u00b0 | 310 |\n| 35.3\u201335.5\u00b0 | 400 |\n| 37.5\u201337.8\u00b0 | 330/411 |\n| 39.86\u00b0 | 420 |\n| 43.6\u201343.8\u00b0 | 422 |\n| 45.75\u00b0 | 510/431 |\n| 51.10\u00b0 | 440 |\n| 52.78\u00b0 | 530/433 |\n| 54.44\u00b0 | 600/442 |\n\nThe cell and space group are substantially more secure than the individual coordinates; Mg/Be ordering is also only weakly constrained by Cu K\u03b1 X-ray intensities because Be scatters very weakly. Neutron diffraction or total-scattering data would be needed to remove that remaining ambiguity.",
